---

1. Executive Summary

The HITS Attendance Alert System is an automated attendance monitoring platform designed to identify students whose subject-wise attendance falls below the required 75% threshold and automatically notify them through SMS.

The system is designed using a modular architecture so that attendance calculation, database management, scheduling, notification delivery, and frontend functionality remain loosely coupled.

The initial prototype will use a simulated ERP dataset rather than directly connecting to the HITS ERP. This allows the development team to validate the complete workflow before implementing institutional ERP integration.

